<http://weee-kg.org/context/scope/00161f8b94616b2ab4c01d77> a weee:ScopeContext ;
    weee:bindingStatus "bound" ;
    weee:description "Spent LIBs manually dismantled into plastic shell, cathode, anode, aluminum foil, etc.; the separated active cathode and anode containing Co and Li were mixed, milled and sieved to <200 µm powder used for bioleaching, with Co at 358 mg/g and Li at 45 mg/g." ;
    weee:evidenceRef "scope:scope-assertion:a4df6f5cbcbf7812:evidence",
        "source:Process Controls for Improving Bioleaching Performance of Both Li and Co from Spent Lithium Ion Batteries at High Pulp Density and its Thermodynamics and Kineti:Product_lithium_ion_battery:entity" ;
    weee:evidenceSpan "The spent LIBs were manually dismantled into different portions including plastic shell, cathode, anode, aluminum foil and so on. Then the separated active cathode and anode containing dense Co and Li were mixed, ground by milling and sieved to obtain a mesh size of less than 200 lm (Mishra et al., 2008a). The resulting powder, used for bioleaching experiments, was digested by HF - HNO _ 3 –HCl method (USEPA, 1996) to determine the content of Co at 358 mg g ^-1 and Li at 45 mg g ^-1 using AAS." ;
    weee:micrographId "Process Controls for Improving Bioleaching Performance of Both Li and Co from Spent Lithium Ion Batteries at High Pulp Density and its Thermodynamics and Kineti" ;
    weee:populationGranularity "batch" ;
    weee:sampleType "spent lithium-ion battery" ;
    weee:scopeDescription "Spent LIBs manually dismantled into plastic shell, cathode, anode, aluminum foil, etc.; the separated active cathode and anode containing Co and Li were mixed, milled and sieved to <200 µm powder used for bioleaching, with Co at 358 mg/g and Li at 45 mg/g." ;
    weee:scopeFacetsJson "{\"population_granularity\": \"batch\", \"sample_type\": \"spent lithium-ion battery\"}" ;
    weee:scopeId "scope-assertion:a4df6f5cbcbf7812" ;
    weee:scopeKind "declared_population" ;
    weee:sourcePaper "Process Controls for Improving Bioleaching Performance of Both Li and Co from Spent Lithium Ion Batteries at High Pulp Density and its Thermodynamics and Kineti" .

