<http://weee-kg.org/context/scope/0ba6350cf700cf28a2c3a6c6> a weee:ScopeContext ;
    weee:bindingStatus "bound" ;
    weee:description "Bioleaching experiments were conducted according to the previous paper (Xin et al., 2009). Unless specifically stated, bioleaching media containing 4.0 g L ^-1 of mixed energy matters (sulfur and pyrite) was inoculated respectively with SOB and IOB as the mixed culture, followed by incubation at 30 C until the pH value dropped to ca 1.0 and the ORP value rose to ca 450 mV. At that time, the spent LIB powder was added into the media to a final concentration of 2% to initiate the bioleaching after its pH value was adjusted precisely to pH 1.0." ;
    weee:evidenceRef "scope:scope-assertion:27ef0e1f89fbe983:evidence",
        "source:Process Controls for Improving Bioleaching Performance of Both Li and Co from Spent Lithium Ion Batteries at High Pulp Density and its Thermodynamics and Kineti:Process_bioleaching_of_Co_and_Li_from_spent_LIB_powder:entity" ;
    weee:evidenceSpan "Bioleaching experiments were conducted according to the previous paper (Xin et al., 2009). Unless specifically stated, bioleaching media containing 4.0 g L ^-1 of mixed energy matters (sulfur and pyrite) was inoculated respectively with SOB and IOB as the mixed culture, followed by incubation at 30 C until the pH value dropped to ca 1.0 and the ORP value rose to ca 450 mV. At that time, the spent LIB powder was added into the media to a final concentration of 2% to initiate the bioleaching after its pH value was adjusted precisely to pH 1.0." ;
    weee:methodFamily "bioleaching" ;
    weee:micrographId "Process Controls for Improving Bioleaching Performance of Both Li and Co from Spent Lithium Ion Batteries at High Pulp Density and its Thermodynamics and Kineti" ;
    weee:scopeDescription "Bioleaching experiments were conducted according to the previous paper (Xin et al., 2009). Unless specifically stated, bioleaching media containing 4.0 g L ^-1 of mixed energy matters (sulfur and pyrite) was inoculated respectively with SOB and IOB as the mixed culture, followed by incubation at 30 C until the pH value dropped to ca 1.0 and the ORP value rose to ca 450 mV. At that time, the spent LIB powder was added into the media to a final concentration of 2% to initiate the bioleaching after its pH value was adjusted precisely to pH 1.0." ;
    weee:scopeFacetsJson "{\"method_family\": \"bioleaching\"}" ;
    weee:scopeId "scope-assertion:27ef0e1f89fbe983" ;
    weee:scopeKind "process_method_family" ;
    weee:sourcePaper "Process Controls for Improving Bioleaching Performance of Both Li and Co from Spent Lithium Ion Batteries at High Pulp Density and its Thermodynamics and Kineti" .

