<http://weee-kg.org/source:Bioleaching%20of%20Valuable%20Metals%20from%20Spent%20Lithium-Ion%20Mobile%20Phone%20Batteries%20Using%20Aspergillus%20Niger:Process_two_step_bioleaching> a weee:Process ;
    rdfs:label "two-step bioleaching" ;
    weee:description "two-step bioleaching is a source-specific Process entity in the study Bioleaching of Valuable Metals from Spent Lithium-Ion Mobile Phone Batteries Using Aspergillus Niger. Scope: In the two-step approach, the fungi were, firstly, pre-cultured in sucrose medium; no battery powder was added until the fungi entered the logarithmic phase. Quantitative observations concern: Al, Co, Cu, Li, Mn." ;
