<http://weee-kg.org/source:Chemical%20Characterisation%20of%20Spent%20Rechargeable%20Batteries:Process_EN_12457_2_leaching_test> a weee:Process ;
    rdfs:label "EN 12457-2 leaching test" ;
    weee:description "EN 12457-2 leaching test is a source-specific Process entity in the study Chemical Characterisation of Spent Rechargeable Batteries. Scope: Leaching tests were performed according to European Standard Procedures (EN – 12457 – 2). All the seven sub-samples (reported in Fig. 1) were put in contact with distilled water in capped bottles. Liquid to solid ratio was 10/1 and the suspension was agitated by an overhead shaker (5 rpm) for 24 h at room temperature (20 ± 5 ^).. Quantitative observations concern: Cd, Co, Cu, Fe, Li." ;
    weee:hasScopeContext <http://weee-kg.org/context/scope/142b7e24750a603e72c57eb1> ;
    rel:hasOutput <http://weee-kg.org/entity/Al>,
        <http://weee-kg.org/entity/K>,
        <http://weee-kg.org/entity/Tl> ;
    rel:hasResultObservation <http://weee-kg.org/source:Chemical%20Characterisation%20of%20Spent%20Rechargeable%20Batteries:Observation_REL_Process_EN_12457_2_leaching_test_HAS_OUTPUT_Material_Cd_e7de13c8982aeacf>,
