<http://weee-kg.org/source:Process%20Controls%20for%20Improving%20Bioleaching%20Performance%20of%20Both%20Li%20and%20Co%20from%20Spent%20Lithium%20Ion%20Batteries%20at%20High%20Pulp%20Density%20and%20its%20Thermodynamics%20and%20Kineti:Process_bioleaching_of_Co_and_Li_from_spent_LIB_powder> a weee:Process ;
    rdfs:label "bioleaching of Co and Li from spent LIB powder" ;
    weee:description "bioleaching of Co and Li from spent LIB powder is a source-specific Process entity in the study Process Controls for Improving Bioleaching Performance of Both Li and Co from Spent Lithium Ion Batteries at High Pulp Density and its Thermodynamics and Kineti. Scope: Bioleaching experiments were conducted according to the previous paper (Xin et al., 2009). Unless specifically stated, bioleaching media containing 4.0 g L ^-1 of mixed energy matters (sulfur and pyrite) was inoculated respectively with SOB and IOB as the mixed culture, followed by incubation at 30 C until the pH value dropped to ca 1.0 and the ORP value rose to ca 450 mV. At that time, the spent LIB powder was added into the media to a final concentration of 2% to initiate the bioleaching after its pH value was adjusted precisely to pH 1.0. Quantitative observations concern: Co, Li." ;
    weee:hasScopeContext <http://weee-kg.org/context/scope/0ba6350cf700cf28a2c3a6c6> ;
    rel:hasResultObservation <http://weee-kg.org/source:Process%20Controls%20for%20Improving%20Bioleaching%20Performance%20of%20Both%20Li%20and%20Co%20from%20Spent%20Lithium%20Ion%20Batteries%20at%20High%20Pulp%20Density%20and%20its%20Thermodynamics%20and%20Kineti:Observation_REL_Process_bioleaching_of_Co_and_Li_from_spent_LIB_powder_HAS_OUTPUT_Material_Co_11a20374a5f5599f>,
