<http://weee-kg.org/source:A%20Combined%20Recovery%20Process%20of%20Metals%20in%20Spent%20Lithium-Ion%20Batteries:Process_hydrochloric_acid_leaching_of_recovered_electrodes> a weee:Process ;
    rdfs:label "hydrochloric acid leaching of recovered electrodes" ;
    weee:description "hydrochloric acid leaching of recovered electrodes is a source-specific Process entity in the study A Combined Recovery Process of Metals in Spent Lithium-Ion Batteries. Scope: Following this sifting, hydrochloric acid was used to dissolve the recovered electrodes, and the influences of duration, temperature, and H+ concentration on leaching efficiency were studied. Quantitative observations concern: Al, Co, Cu, Fe, Li." ;
