<http://weee-kg.org/source:Bioleaching%20of%20Valuable%20Metals%20from%20Spent%20Lithium-Ion%20Mobile%20Phone%20Batteries%20Using%20Aspergillus%20Niger:Process_chemical_leaching> a weee:Process ;
    rdfs:label "chemical leaching" ;
    weee:description "chemical leaching is a source-specific Process entity in the study Bioleaching of Valuable Metals from Spent Lithium-Ion Mobile Phone Batteries Using Aspergillus Niger. Scope: Chemical leaching of the spent battery powder was carried out to evaluate the leaching effectiveness of organic acids through the use of a mixture of commercial citric acid, oxalic acid, malic acid and gluconic acid at a concentration similar to the bioleaching experiment." ;
    weee:hasScopeContext <http://weee-kg.org/context/scope/2c67ea724e2723cb628c9a83> ;
    rel:memberOfMethodFamily <http://weee-kg.org/anchor:MethodFamily:chemical_leaching> .

<http://weee-kg.org/source:Bioleaching%20of%20Valuable%20Metals%20from%20Spent%20Lithium-Ion%20Mobile%20Phone%20Batteries%20Using%20Aspergillus%20Niger:Process_one_step_bioleaching> a weee:Process ;
    rdfs:label "one-step bioleaching" ;
    weee:description "one-step bioleaching is a source-specific Process entity in the study Bioleaching of Valuable Metals from Spent Lithium-Ion Mobile Phone Batteries Using Aspergillus Niger. Scope: In the one-step bioleaching process, 1 mL of spore suspension was inoculated into sucrose medium (containing battery powder) and incubated for 30 days. Quantitative observations concern: Al, Cu, Li, Mn." ;
    weee:hasScopeContext <http://weee-kg.org/context/scope/ac7a27f3286f109a3ec47c27> ;
    rel:hasResultObservation <http://weee-kg.org/source:Bioleaching%20of%20Valuable%20Metals%20from%20Spent%20Lithium-Ion%20Mobile%20Phone%20Batteries%20Using%20Aspergillus%20Niger:Observation_REL_Process_one_step_bioleaching_HAS_OUTPUT_Material_Al_49af1dd0f9c29231>,
