<http://weee-kg.org/source:Leaching%20Lithium%20from%20the%20Anode%20Electrode%20Materials%20of%20Spent%20Lithium-Ion%20Batteries%20by%20Hydrochloric%20Acid%20%28Hcl%29:Process_reductive_hydrochloric_acid_leaching_of_calcined_powder> a weee:Process ;
    rdfs:label "reductive hydrochloric acid leaching of calcined powder" ;
    weee:description "reductive hydrochloric acid leaching of calcined powder is a source-specific Process entity in the study Leaching Lithium from the Anode Electrode Materials of Spent Lithium-Ion Batteries by Hydrochloric Acid (Hcl). Scope: In this study, hydrochloric acid was taken as leachate to recycle lithium from the calcined powder materials. To increase the leaching efficiency, reductive leaching was carried out with H2O2 as the reducing agent. Quantitative observations concern: Li." ;
    weee:hasScopeContext <http://weee-kg.org/context/scope/36bd9677cb470c3981aed967> ;
    rel:hasResultObservation <http://weee-kg.org/source:Leaching%20Lithium%20from%20the%20Anode%20Electrode%20Materials%20of%20Spent%20Lithium-Ion%20Batteries%20by%20Hydrochloric%20Acid%20%28Hcl%29:Observation_REL_Process_reductive_hydrochloric_acid_leaching_of_calcined_powder_HAS_OUTPUT_Material_Li_0f913b6cda8c44c0>,
