<http://weee-kg.org/source:Recovery%20of%20Cobalt%20as%20Cobalt%20Oxalate%20from%20Spent%20Lithium%20Ion%20Batteries%20by%20Using%20Glycine%20as%20Leaching%20Agent:Process_LiCoO2_dissolution_in_glycine_and_ascorbic_acid> a weee:Process ;
    rdfs:label "LiCoO2 dissolution in glycine and ascorbic acid" ;
    weee:description "LiCoO2 dissolution in glycine and ascorbic acid is a source-specific Process entity in the study Recovery of Cobalt as Cobalt Oxalate from Spent Lithium Ion Batteries by Using Glycine as Leaching Agent. Scope: The above cathode material (LiCoO2, 0.2: g) was subjected for chemical dissolution using mild organic acids, an aqueous mixture of glycine and ascorbic acid were taken in a three necked roundbottomed flask with volume of100 mL and the flask was placed in a water bath to control the reaction temperature during the leaching. Quantitative observations concern: Co." ;
    weee:hasScopeContext <http://weee-kg.org/context/scope/627f822ac79d26fe65c52e55> ;
    rel:hasResultObservation <http://weee-kg.org/source:Recovery%20of%20Cobalt%20as%20Cobalt%20Oxalate%20from%20Spent%20Lithium%20Ion%20Batteries%20by%20Using%20Glycine%20as%20Leaching%20Agent:Observation_REL_Process_LiCoO2_dissolution_in_glycine_and_ascorbic_acid_HAS_OUTPUT_Material_Co_05097b088c4eccb8>,
