    rdfs:label "aqua regia leaching of intact PCB and electronic components" ;
    weee:description "aqua regia leaching of intact PCB and electronic components is a source-specific Process entity in the study A Comprehensive Characterization of End-of-Life Mobile Phones for Secondary Material Resources Identification. Scope: In order to determine the metal content into the electronic part of MPs, a first leaching of the intact PCB and electronic components was performed at 25 C using aqua regia (a solution of concentrated HNO and concentrated HCl 1/3 v/v)." ;
    weee:hasScopeContext <http://weee-kg.org/context/scope/9c88d0e0a2e5816a3448645d> ;
    rel:memberOfMethodFamily <http://weee-kg.org/anchor:MethodFamily:aqua_regia_leaching> .

<http://weee-kg.org/source:A%20Promising%20Physical%20Method%20for%20Recovery%20of%20Licoo%202%20and%20Graphite%20from%20Spent%20Lithium-Ion%20Batteries%20Grinding%20Flotation:Process_grinding_flotation> a weee:Process ;
    rdfs:label "grinding flotation" ;
    weee:description "grinding flotation is a source-specific Process entity in the study A Promising Physical Method for Recovery of Licoo 2 and Graphite from Spent Lithium-Ion Batteries Grinding Flotation. Scope: Grinding flotation experiments were carried out in standard Hardgrove apparatus and lab-scale flotation machine. First, 40 g of mixed electrode powder together with steel balls were sealed in the grinding chamber. The grinding times were 2.5 min, 5 min, 10 min, 20 min and 30 min, respectively. Then, the grinding productions were subjected to reverse flotation with the same experimental conditions. Quantitative observations concern: LiCoO2, graphite." ;
    weee:hasScopeContext <http://weee-kg.org/context/scope/c64d18a2b06ba90d04fac347> ;
    rel:hasOutput <http://weee-kg.org/entity/graphite%20flake> ;
